@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Deploying to Azure App Services";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Azure App Services is a **fully managed platform** for deploying web applications, APIs, and mobile backends. Azure DevOps enables seamless deployment to Azure App Services using **Release Pipelines**.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Use Azure App Services?</h2>
        <p>Azure App Services provides a **scalable, secure, and easy-to-manage** hosting environment for applications.</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Supports multiple languages like **.NET, Java, Python, Node.js, PHP, and Ruby**.</li>
            <li>Built-in **auto-scaling** and high availability.</li>
            <li>Integrated **CI/CD with Azure DevOps**.</li>
            <li>**Secure and compliant** with enterprise security standards.</li>
            <li>Provides **custom domains, SSL certificates, and deployment slots**.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/media/app-service-overview.png" alt="Azure App Services Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Overview of Azure App Services</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Deployment Models</h4>
            <ul>
                <li>**Manual Deployment** – Upload files directly using FTP or the Azure Portal.</li>
                <li>**Azure DevOps CI/CD Pipelines** – Automate deployments via pipelines.</li>
                <li>**GitHub Actions** – Deploy from GitHub repositories.</li>
                <li>**Container-based Deployment** – Deploy Docker containers to Azure App Services.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Steps to Deploy an Application to Azure App Services</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to set up **continuous deployment** using Azure DevOps:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Create an App Service:</strong> In Azure Portal, create a new App Service instance.</li>
            <li><strong>Connect to Azure DevOps:</strong> Set up a service connection in Azure DevOps.</li>
            <li><strong>Define Build Pipeline:</strong> Create a **build pipeline** to generate artifacts.</li>
            <li><strong>Configure Release Pipeline:</strong> Use Azure DevOps to deploy artifacts to the App Service.</li>
            <li><strong>Trigger Deployment:</strong> Automatically deploy on code changes.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Example YAML for Deploying to Azure App Service</h4>
            <pre>
stages:
- stage: Deploy
  displayName: 'Deploy to Azure App Service'
  jobs:
  - deployment: DeployWebApp
    environment: 'Production'
    strategy:
      runOnce:
        deploy:
          steps:
          - task: AzureWebApp@1
            inputs:
              azureSubscription: 'AzureServiceConnection'
              appName: 'my-web-app'
              package: '$(Pipeline.Workspace)/drop/*.zip'
            </pre>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/app-service/media/deploy-app-service.png" alt="Deploying to Azure App Service" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Deploying to Azure App Service Using Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Best Practices for Deploying to Azure App Services</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Use **deployment slots** for staging and testing before going live.</li>
            <li>Enable **auto-scaling** to handle traffic spikes.</li>
            <li>Implement **role-based access control (RBAC)** for security.</li>
            <li>Monitor performance using **Azure Application Insights**.</li>
            <li>Enable **zero-downtime deployments** using blue-green strategies.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Deploying applications to **Azure App Services** using **Azure DevOps Pipelines** simplifies **automated deployments, scaling, and monitoring**. By implementing best practices, teams can ensure smooth and reliable software releases.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Approvals & Gates in Azure Pipelines** to enforce controlled deployments.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("StagesJobsTasks", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Stages, Jobs & Tasks</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("ApprovalsGates", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Approvals & Gates &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>
